  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## What tracing answers that today's monitoring cannot\n\nEach row below is a question an operator or a user asks about a download.\n\n- **Left**: the question, and why it cannot be answered today.\n- **Middle**: the closest thing Pelican's existing monitoring offers (its Prometheus `/metrics`).\n- **Right**: the answer, computed from the spans every service now records.\n\nThe federation behind this page is the demo's: one director, one Go-native origin, one Go-native cache, and an exerciser downloading objects in a loop.\nTo follow one download from end to end, open the **Pelican download lookup** page (top right) or click any trace ID below."
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "1. A download was slow. Where did the time go?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The question.** A user says a download took too long. Was it finding the federation, asking the director, probing caches, waiting on the cache, or checking the checksum?\n\n**Today.** Each server measures only its own requests. Nothing measures the client, and nothing ties one server's request to another's. The transfer ad has a total, and its time to first byte is always 0.\n\n**With tracing.** The client's own spans divide each download into stages."
      },
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Today: average request time, per server",
      "description": "pelican_http_request_duration_seconds. Only the origin exports it; it says nothing about the client, the director or the cache, and nothing about any one download.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "pelican-metrics"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "pelican-metrics"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (server_type) (rate(pelican_http_request_duration_seconds_sum[5m])) / sum by (server_type) (rate(pelican_http_request_duration_seconds_count[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{server_type}} request"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 4,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "With tracing: average time per stage of a download",
      "description": "Average duration of each client stage over the last 5 minutes. client.attempt is the transfer itself; the rest is overhead.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "pelican-metrics"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "pelican-metrics"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (span_name) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_sum{service_name=\"pelican-client\",span_name=~\"client\\\\.(discover_federation|query_director|acquire_token|sort_attempts|attempt|verify_checksum)\"}[5m])) / sum by (span_name) (rate(traces_span_metrics_duration_milliseconds_count{service_name=\"pelican-client\",span_name=~\"client\\\\.(discover_federation|query_director|acquire_token|sort_attempts|attempt|verify_checksum)\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{span_name}}",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "displayMode": "basic",
        "valueMode": "color",
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "namePlacement": "left",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "values": false,
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": ""
        },
        "minVizHeight": 16,
        "maxVizHeight": 40,
        "text": {
          "titleSize": 13,
          "valueSize": 18
        }
      },
      "id": 5,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "2. Was it a cache hit or a miss, and what does a miss cost?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 6,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The question.** Is the cache doing its job? How many requests does it serve from disk, and how much slower is one it has to fetch?\n\n**Today.** The director counts how many clients it *sent* to a cache. The Go-native cache exports no request metric at all, so nothing says whether those requests were hits.\n\n**With tracing.** Every cache request records its result, so hits and misses can be counted and timed separately."
      },
      "id": 7,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 17
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Today: clients the director sent to a cache",
      "description": "pelican_director_redirects_total. A count of redirects; what the cache then did is invisible.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "pelican-metrics"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "pelican-metrics"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (destination) (rate(pelican_director_redirects_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "redirected to {{destination}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 8,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 17
      }
    },
