    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "5. A download failed. Which hop failed, and with what error?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 20,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The question.** A user reports a failed download. Did the director refuse it, did the cache fail, or did the origin not have the object?\n\n**Today.** Each server counts its own error responses. The origin's 404s below could be a user's typo or a broken federation; nothing says which downloads they belong to.\n\n**With tracing.** A failed download is one trace. The spans that failed are marked, with the error attached, down to the hop that returned it."
      },
      "id": 21,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 47
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Today: error responses, per server",
      "description": "pelican_http_requests_total with a 4xx or 5xx code. Counts, with no link to a download.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "pelican-metrics"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "pelican-metrics"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (server_type, method, code) (rate(pelican_http_requests_total{code=~\"4..|5..\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{server_type}} {{method}} {{code}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none"
            }
          }
