    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "8. Which log lines belong to this download?",
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": [],
      "id": 34,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 76
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The question.** Something went wrong with one download. What did each server log about it?\n\n**Today.** Search each server's log by time and object path, and hope the clocks agree and nothing else touched that object.\n\n**With tracing.** The origin, the cache and the client write the trace ID on their request log lines. Logs are not collected centrally, but on each server one search for the trace ID finds that server's lines exactly."
      },
      "id": 35,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 77
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Today: nothing\n\nLogs are per server and carry no shared identifier for a plain download.\n\n`X-Pelican-JobId` joins them only for HTCondor jobs, and not at the director, which replaces it with its own ID."
      },
      "id": 36,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 77
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": 37,
      "title": "With tracing: one download's log lines, on each service",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 77
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Take a trace ID from any table above, then:\n\n```\nmake trace-logs id=<trace id>\n```\n\nor, on one service:\n\n```\ndocker compose exec cache grep 'trace_id=<trace id>' /var/log/pelican/cache.log\ndocker compose exec origin grep 'trace_id=<trace id>' /var/log/pelican/origin.log\ndocker compose exec exerciser grep 'trace_id=<trace id>' /var/log/pelican/client.log\n```\n\nThe director's lines carry its own request ID instead, which is `pelican.job_id` on its `director.redirect` span."
      }
    }
  ]
